{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "G4 audio \u2014 the POSITIONAL ATTENUATION FOLD (dsx-game.md \u00a72 G4). Pure math in the shared kernel: a listener position, a source position and the three knobs fold to {distance, gain, pan}. The model is the clamped INVERSE-DISTANCE law (gain = ref / (ref + rolloff \u00b7 (clamp(d, ref, max) \u2212 ref))) \u2014 the same curve the Web Audio 'inverse' panner uses, so a web renderer can hand the numbers straight to a PannerNode. pan is the listener-relative X component (dx / d), clamped to [-1, 1], and 0 when the source sits on the listener. PLAYBACK of the folded numbers is NOT part of this rung (the named absence) \u2014 Core/Audio plays SFX/music unattenuated.",
